linux-cv181x-sodoport (7.0-15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial recipe-only Debian packaging for the Milk-V Duo 256M kernel.
  * Prepare uscan/gbp import flow for upstream Linux 7.0.
  * Seed the board kernel config from the local sg2002 Alpine packaging draft.
  * Add an initial DTS patch for the SG2002 Milk-V Duo 256M board.
  * Add a Debian-oriented config fragment scaffold for future config refreshes.
  * Rename the packaged kernel flavour to cv181x-sodoport.
  * Add a linux-source-cv181x-sodoport binary package.
  * Switch to Debian-style kernel packaging with a versioned image package,
    standard /boot artifact layout, and kernel maintainer hook integration.
  * Keep DTB installation generic and move board-specific u-boot-menu policy
    back out of the kernel package so board support packages can choose DTBs
    via U-Boot's fdtfile mechanism.
  * Keep packaged modules compressed with Zstd.
  * Fix DTB installation paths so synced /boot DTBs match u-boot-menu lookups.
  * Mark cross-build tools as native build dependencies so sbuild resolves the
    amd64 toolchain instead of trying to install them as riscv64 packages.
  * Replace debhelper-compat with a native debhelper dependency to avoid
    cross-resolver issues with the compat virtual package.
  * Declare debhelper compatibility via debian/compat so source package
    generation does not rely on dh inheriting DH_COMPAT from debian/rules.
  * Make the CI sbuild wrapper use native helper dependencies for cross builds
    so Ubuntu's runner package does not try to satisfy dumb-init for the
    target architecture.
  * Remove the throw-away chroot's external apt solver before dependency
    installation so cross-builds fall back to plain apt instead of crashing
    on the runner's mismatched solver binary.
  * Disable the uninstallable build-dependency explainer in CI so genuine
    dependency failures report directly from the install step.
  * Install sbuild from Ubuntu 24.04 backports in GitHub Actions so the
    runner uses a version that includes the dumb-init and cross-resolver
    fixes missing from noble-updates 0.85.10ubuntu0.2.
  * Stop forcing :native on Multi-Arch: foreign build tools so
    dpkg-checkbuilddeps accepts the native packages that sbuild installs
    during cross builds. Keep :native only for native -dev packages that
    must stay on the build architecture.
  * Add missing kernel build tools for Debian-style packaging by declaring
    openssl and zstd in Build-Depends-Arch, matching the current config's
    compressed-module install path more closely to Debian's linux source
    package.
  * Build and publish versioned plus meta kernel headers packages with
    standard /usr/src and /lib/modules/<version>/{build,source} layout for
    external module builds.
  * Run a separate native sbuild pass for Architecture: all packages so the
    linux-source package is built and published alongside the cross-built
    kernel image and headers.
  * Ship a Debian-owned package README in the generated source tree so
    dh_installdocs no longer depends on the recipe branch's README filename.

 -- Packaging Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>  Sat, 18 Apr 2026 01:34:00 +0900
